# ============================================================================
# SECRETS — never commit a credential to this repo.
# Credentials live OUTSIDE every git repo, in ~/.credentials/charlie_kirk.json
# (mode 600), and are read at run time by
# site/docs/Planes/following/apis/public_open_source/code/lib/credentials.js.
# These patterns are the backstop, not the policy.
# ============================================================================
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!*.public.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
credentials.json
!site/docs/Planes/following/apis/public_open_source/code/lib/credentials.js
service-account*.json
*credentials*.yaml
*secrets*.yaml
.netrc
cookies.txt
**/captures/**/cookies*.json

npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Local research notes
Research/Charlie_Kirk.txt

# IPFS videos directory
IPFS/videos/

# videos/ — the media never lands in the repo (it is pulled from IPFS), but the
# metadata that describes it must travel with the repo. Use "videos/*" rather
# than "videos/" so the negations below can re-include named files; git will not
# re-include anything inside a directory that is itself excluded.
# videos.yaml is the video evidence hierarchy, the counterpart of
# images/images.yaml. Add a new negation here rather than force-adding by hand.
videos/*
!videos/.gitignore
!videos/videos.yaml
!videos/manifest.yaml
!videos/videos.md

