# ============================================================================
# IMAGES ARE TRACKED IN GIT — DO NOT ADD PER-FILE IMAGE IGNORE LINES HERE.
# ============================================================================
# These directories must stay fully tracked. The Docusaurus build and the live
# site at whoassassinatedcharliekirk.com serve files straight out of them, so an
# ignored file becomes a broken image in production:
#
#   images/                                   source images (private layer)
#   site/internals/static/img/evidence/       served as /img/evidence/<sha>.jpg
#   site/internals/static/img/video_posters/  served as /img/video_posters/...
#
# Large File Bridge previously appended ~1,950 per-file lines for these paths.
# Those were harmless for files already committed (git never un-tracks a tracked
# file) but silently dropped any NEW image, which is how two images went missing
# on 2026-08-12. All such lines were removed. Do not let them come back.
#
# To keep an image OUT of the repo or off the public site, use the real gates:
#   images/.gitignore                      per-file privacy exclusions
#   images/ban_images.csv                  publish-time ban (see CLAUDE.md)
#   image_planning/exclude_images.txt      legacy sha256 never-publish list
#
# Videos are the exception: videos/* stays ignored on purpose (pulled from IPFS).
# ============================================================================

# Python bytecode caches — build artifacts, never committed.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

